node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
.expo-shared/
*.log
*.bak

# Signing keystores / credentials — must NEVER be committed. Losing this key or
# leaking it means anyone can sign APKs impersonating the app. Keep it in secure
# storage (EAS credentials / an encrypted backup), not in the repo.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
GoogleService-Info.plist

# NOTE: google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the Android FCM
# *client* config — not a secret: it ships inside every APK and is extractable
# from any published build. Ignoring it silently broke Android push for weeks:
# the file was force-added so git tracked it (git archive showed it), but EAS
# Build applies .gitignore literally when uploading, so it never reached the
# builder. The google-services gradle plugin was then never applied and the APK
# shipped without Firebase → "Default FirebaseApp is not initialized" →
# getExpoPushTokenAsync failed → no Android push token was ever registered.
# Real secrets (keystores, .p8/.p12) stay ignored above.

# Native projects — Continuous Native Generation. Regenerated by
# `expo prebuild`, so they aren't committed. The leading slash anchors these to
# the app root, so source targets/modules (e.g. modules/live-activity/ios,
# targets/rideactivity) are NOT affected.
/ios/
/android/

